@@ -647,7 +647,7 @@
       ],
       "decided_utc": "2026-09-27T15:30:00Z",
       "decided_by": "lane-296 collision maker (Opus 5.5), pending HQ Sol re-check",
-      "owed": "partial: iq3_xxs 5120x6x17408 U8 vs r86i +2.7% (18 paired rounds, 13 slower, 95% CI [1.008,1.047]); GPU-execution side, same kernel/pipeline/dispatch; mechanism ASSUMED (barrier/sync or buffer placement), bisect owed lane-298; served cost = gpu-run26 stage b",
+      "owed": "partial: iq3_xxs 5120x6x17408 U8 vs r86i +2.7% (18 paired rounds, 13 slower, 95% CI [1.008,1.047]); GPU-execution side; kernel, pipeline creation, selection, dispatch args, per-node sync, submit batching and the test harness all identical to r86i (CHECKED); mechanism ASSUMED (descriptor/buffer placement or command-buffer handling), bisect owed lane-298; width n=6 is NOT dispatched on the registered GSQ line (DFlash2 depth 4 = verify n=5); documented op-level loss for ruling",
       "lane296_b1_close": {
         "ours": "MEASURED iq3 n=7 cells (run17): R 101/966/1668/1584 us (iq3_s 1024/10240/17408x5120, 5120x17408).",
         "union": "MEASURED: U8 101/959/1648/1587 us; U8/R median 0.997 [0.980, 1.007] over 12 n=7 cells; N7_ROWS=4 arm (= the registered legacy value that carries the n=7 register-spill cliff, registered 22.1x at 248320) 2036/20288/34597/39268 us = default/off median 0.398, the cliff fix holds on U8. The 248320 n=7 decider cell R vs U8 is OPEN (gpu-run24 stage d). Sign hoist v2 default/legacy median 1.000 over 96 cells (run17), 1.001 (run23 g) = wall-clock neutral on gfx1103, as registered. Open cells: iq3_xxs 5120x6x17408, 10240x3x5120, 1024x2x5120 (see lane296_b1_close.open).",
@@ -659,7 +659,7 @@
         ],
         "open": "lane-296 run24 close 2026-09-28 18:5x (ev24, R/U8/V ABBA x6 op cells; sx8 n512 x4; hoist x3; head x3; 47/47 rc=0). Parser note: R prints two banner lines between name and timing on some cells; the old one-gap regex dropped R iq3_xxs 10240x3x5120 in run24 only (rerun of b1g_read/b1win over ev19/ev17 with the fixed regex: output unchanged). V MISSING on iq3_s 5120x{1,6}x17408, iq4_xs 17408x{6,7}x5120, q5_K 5120x3x17408, q5_K 1024x7x5120: shapes absent from the vanilla-wt harness patch; cure = add the cases + a short leg, owed on HQ word. ORDER EFFECT (measured, CELL block where R alternates first/last): U8/R geo 0.986 when R runs first vs 1.005 when R runs last = the FIRST leg of a round runs ~2.0% slower (+-1.4% 1 SE, ASSUMED-level); consistent with q4_K 248320x4x5120 U8 vs U8 GGML_ARIFI_Q4K_W5_SPLIT=0 1.030 3/3 on the SAME pipeline (split admits n=5,6 only, ggml-vulkan.cpp:6899; w5off always last). In the hoist block r86i ALWAYS ran first (gpu-run24.sh:37), so that order FAVOURS U8: any U8-slower hoist cell is understated, and hoist-block ties/wins are not counterbalanced. KERNEL IDENTITY (CHECKED 18:5x, U8 build-vk SPIR-V blobs minus 20-byte header byte-searched in r86i test-backend-ops.exe): mul_mat_vec_{iq3_xxs,iq3_s,iq4_xs,q5_k,q4_k,sx8} f32/f16/q8_1 variants and quantize_q8_1{,_x4} all present = same kernels; iq3_xxs mat-vec pipeline creation lines identical e86ca0289a..HEAD. So every U8-vs-r86i op delta on these cells is OUTSIDE the kernel (host submission/sync path of the b10825->b11178 rework, or the test-backend-ops perf loop). receipts cache/lane296/ev24 (reader b24_read.py -> b24_read.out, multiline parser fix 18:4x), ev23h/SVP-plain-RvsU8.txt.",
         "run24": "iq3_xxs 5120x6x17408 us r86i 1374.8 / vanilla 1497.3 / U8 1382.0 (run24 medians); paired U8/R stage g + run24 geo 1.031 CI [1.001,1.063] = U8 LOSES ~3% to r86i, WINS 7.3% vs vanilla (U8/V 0.927, 0/6 slower). MECHANISM NARROWED (CHECKED 18:5x): the kernel is NOT the cause. iq3_xxs has no q8_1 mat-vec; the dispatched kernel is mul_mat_vec_iq3_xxs_f32_f32(_subgroup/_no_shmem), whose U8 SPIR-V (minus header) is byte-present in r86i test-backend-ops.exe; iq3_xxs pipeline-creation lines (spec constants, rows, wg) identical e86ca0289a..HEAD; route banner identical. So the ~3% is host-side (submission/sync path of the b10825->b11178 rework, or the upstream test-backend-ops perf loop), same GPU work. Decider for the side = gpu-run25.sh c (GGML_VK_PERF_LOGGER per-dispatch kernel time R vs U8, ~3 min) + b (8 more ABBA rounds); owed on HQ word. Order effect (common note) is balanced here (ABBA), so it does not explain this cell. Other cells TIE: iq3_xxs 10240x3x5120 r86i 571.9 / vanilla 569.7 / U8 574.1 (U8/R 1.003, U8/V 1.008 5/6 = 0.8%); 1024x2x5120 67.1 / 70.0 / 68.7 (1.000 / 0.999); head 248320x7x5120 iq3_xxs 17977.5 / not in leg / 17800.6 (0.999), iq3_s 20896.7 / - / 20818.0 (0.992).",
-        "run25": "iq3_xxs 5120x6x17408 us r86i 1374.8 / vanilla 1497.3 / U8 1382.0 (run24 medians); U8 wins 7.3% vs vanilla. run25 b ABBA x8 U8/R 1.022 CI [0.993,1.052] 5/8; pooled 18 rounds 1.027 CI [1.008,1.047]. No order effect in this cell (U8 first 1.025, R first 1.020). SIDE: perf logger = GPU timestamps (writeTimestamp eAllCommands, ggml-vulkan.cpp:16596/16948/16990); host gap (us/run minus logger steady median) r86i 79.8/79.3 us, U8 76.2/76.8 us (n=2/arm) = host submission NOT the carrier; logger U8/R flips 1.042/0.987 (n=2). DISPATCH IDENTITY (CHECKED 19:5x): ggml_vk_get_dequantize_mul_mat_vec r86i 6fb7a425a:10749 vs U8 :6778 differ only by a TQ1_0 case; ggml_vk_mul_mat_vec_q_f16 r86i :13037 vs U8 :8367 only by swap_inputs (false on MUL_MAT); with the 18:5x SPIR-V + pipeline-creation identity: same kernel, pipeline, grid, push constants. Remaining suspects ASSUMED: b11178 barrier/sync placement (eAllCommands timestamps include barrier stalls) or test-backend-ops buffer placement. LINE EXPOSURE (gguf reader): GSQ IQ3_S has 7 iq3_xxs ffn_down tensors of this shape (upper bound 7 x ~39 us = ~0.27 ms/step at n=6); Huihui Q4_K_XL has none. receipts cache/lane296/ev25 (28/28 rc=0; readers b25_read.py, b25_order.py)"
+        "run25": "iq3_xxs 5120x6x17408 us r86i 1374.8 / vanilla 1497.3 / U8 1382.0 (run24 medians); U8 wins 7.3% vs vanilla. run25 b ABBA x8 U8/R 1.022 CI [0.993,1.052] 5/8; pooled 18 rounds 1.027 CI [1.008,1.047]. No order effect in this cell (U8 first 1.025, R first 1.020). SIDE: perf logger = GPU timestamps (writeTimestamp eAllCommands, ggml-vulkan.cpp:16596/16948/16990); host gap (us/run minus logger steady median) r86i 79.8/79.3 us, U8 76.2/76.8 us (n=2/arm) = host submission NOT the carrier; logger U8/R flips 1.042/0.987 (n=2). DISPATCH IDENTITY (CHECKED 19:5x): ggml_vk_get_dequantize_mul_mat_vec r86i 6fb7a425a:10749 vs U8 :6778 differ only by a TQ1_0 case; ggml_vk_mul_mat_vec_q_f16 r86i :13037 vs U8 :8367 only by swap_inputs (false on MUL_MAT); with the 18:5x SPIR-V + pipeline-creation identity: same kernel, pipeline, grid, push constants. ALSO CHECKED 20:0x: test-backend-ops test_mul_mat case and eval_perf loop identical (U8 adds reinit_perf_iter, a no-op for MUL_MAT, outside the timed region); per-node sync decision (overlaps_unsynced block) identical; ggml_backend_vk_graph_compute submit/batching identical except fusion patterns that do not match a lone MUL_MAT and debug labels gated by GGML_VK_DEBUG_MARKERS (unset = inert); ggml_vk_create_pipeline_func identical. Remaining suspects ASSUMED: ggml_vk_dispatch_pipeline internals (descriptor-set handling), buffer memory placement, command-buffer management of the b11178 rework. LINE EXPOSURE (gguf reader): GSQ IQ3_S has 7 iq3_xxs ffn_down tensors of this shape (upper bound 7 x ~39 us = ~0.27 ms/step at n=6); Huihui Q4_K_XL has none. The registered GSQ DFlash2 line runs depth 4 (R86 record 8.118 t/s) = verify width n=5, so n=6 is off the registered served path (depth 5 only); gpu-run26 stage b runs depth 4 on both arms. receipts cache/lane296/ev25 (28/28 rc=0; readers b25_read.py, b25_order.py)"
       }
